## 2. Key source code (verbatim relevant parts)

### Household id computation — `Household.java`
Keys the household on **lastName + address** (normalized: trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case), SHA-256, first 8 bytes as 16 upper-case hex chars:
```java
public static String normalize(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return "";
    }
    return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
}

public static String id(String lastName, String address) {
    String key = normalize(lastName) + "|" + normalize(address);
    try {
        byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256").digest(key.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(16);
        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
            sb.append(String.format("%02X", digest[i]));
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }
    catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 not available", e);
    }
}
```

### Duplicate detection (hard) — `OwnerIdentity.java` + `RequireUniqueIdentity.java`
The single consolidated identity key is `normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`, but the **duplicate collision test uses only `contactKey` = telephone+email** (householdId is NOT part of the collision test):
```java
// OwnerIdentity.java
public static String key(String telephone, String email, String lastName, String address) {
    return contactKey(telephone, email) + "|" + Household.id(lastName, address);
}

public static String contactKey(String telephone, String email) {
    return normalizedTelephone(telephone) + "|" + normalizeEmail(email);
}
```
```java
// RequireUniqueIdentity.java — throws DuplicateIdentityException (409)
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateIdentityException {
    String contactKey = OwnerIdentity.contactKey(request.getTelephone(), request.getEmail());
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        String existingKey = OwnerIdentity.contactKey(existing.getTelephone(), existing.getEmail());
        if (contactKey.equals(existingKey)) {
            throw new DuplicateIdentityException(
                    "An owner with the same identity already exists");
        }
    }
}
```

### Soft duplicate — `FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`
Flags (not rejects) when last name + postcode match an existing owner but the telephone differs; records earliest matching id:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String lastName = owner.getLastName();
    String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
    String telephone = OwnerIdentity.normalizedTelephone(owner.getTelephone());
    Integer matchId = null;
    if (postcode != null && !postcode.isBlank()) {
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (existing.getId() == null || !lastName.equalsIgnoreCase(existing.getLastName())
                    || !postcode.equals(existing.getPostcode())) {
                continue;
            }
            if (telephone.equals(OwnerIdentity.normalizedTelephone(existing.getTelephone()))) {
                continue; // same telephone: a hard duplicate, not a possible one
            }
            if (matchId == null || existing.getId() < matchId) {
                matchId = existing.getId();
            }
        }
    }
    owner.setPossibleDuplicate(matchId != null);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(matchId);
}
```

### Household member count — `CountHouseholdMembers.java`
Counts existing owners with the same householdId and stores `householdSize = existing + 1`:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String householdId = Household.id(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
    int existing = 0;
    for (Owner other : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (householdId.equals(Household.id(other.getLastName(), other.getAddress()))) {
            existing++;
        }
    }
    owner.setHouseholdSize(existing + 1);
}
```

### Membership level — `MembershipLevel.java`
Starts at 1; +1 if email present; +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`; capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure, not awarded):
```java
public static int of(Integer namesakeCount, String email) {
    int level = 1;
    boolean hasEmail = email != null && !email.isBlank();
    if (hasEmail) {
        level++;
    }
    boolean unique = namesakeCount != null && namesakeCount == 0;
    if (unique) {
        level++;
    }
    return Math.min(level, 3);
}
```

